(342644, 25821, 6870, '<td valign="top">Hi David. I''m not sure how this got way back here. I suppose it could use more light on the guy, but the photo still works. Unfortunately, most folks don''t look for more than a few seconds (like 2 or 3!), so subtle shots like this, which are good, don''t get the attention they deserve. Keep up the good work!</td>', 'Hi David. I''m not sure how this got way back here. I suppose it could use more light on the guy, but the photo still works. Unfortunately, most folks don''t look for more than a few seconds (like 2 or 3!), so subtle shots like this, which are good, don''t get the attention they deserve. Keep up the good work!', '2003-06-30 11:48:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(342714, 25957, 5333, '<td valign="top">Chef mieka? lol<br/>I''ve used to work in a hotel kitchen. Looks like they are preparing for a function?<br/></td>', 'Chef mieka? lolI''ve used to work in a hotel kitchen. Looks like they are preparing for a function?', '2003-06-30 13:30:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(342783, 25979, 8159, '<td valign="top">The long shadows and yellowish cast were caused by the sun being low on the horizon because of it being late in the day (the start of the show was only a couple hours away). The fire marshall wouldn''t permit me to use a flash (and I wasn''t about to argue with him.) It was fun to see the stuff up-close and talk to the fireworks crew. And I got a few nice shots of the show (from a regular viewing distance, not at the launch site) a few hours later.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-06-30 13:25:50.</i></td>', 'The long shadows and yellowish cast were caused by the sun being low on the horizon because of it being late in the day (the start of the show was only a couple hours away). The fire marshall wouldn''t permit me to use a flash (and I wasn''t about to argue with him.) It was fun to see the stuff up-close and talk to the fireworks crew. And I got a few nice shots of the show (from a regular viewing distance, not at the launch site) a few hours later.', '2003-06-30 14:23:35.000000', '2003-06-30 14:25:50.000000', 0),
(342850, 25589, 1863, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Hi SharQ<br/> <br/>Let''s get straight to business.. Does this meet the challenge? Yup, definitely. How often do you get to see people flying planes?<br/> <br/>All the technical things you did here are superb, the fast shutter speed, the iso, and the aperture. I can''t think of anything I would have done differently. It''s a shame that we cannot control the actual circumstances when we take pictures. I think what would have helped get a better score, would be to have some clouds (lol), or something interesting, but not too distracting.<br/> <br/>I like this picture, I gave it a very high score. Good luck in future challenges, I always enjoy your pictures.<br/>-Annida</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. Hi SharQ Let''s get straight to business.. Does this meet the challenge? Yup, definitely. How often do you get to see people flying planes? All the technical things you did here are superb, the fast shutter speed, the iso, and the aperture. I can''t think of anything I would have done differently. It''s a shame that we cannot control the actual circumstances when we take pictures. I think what would have helped get a better score, would be to have some clouds (lol), or something interesting, but not too distracting. I like this picture, I gave it a very high score. Good luck in future challenges, I always enjoy your pictures.-Annida', '2003-06-30 15:13:45.000000', NULL, 0),
