(343095, 25434, 6870, '<td valign="top">I''m glad this placed well, but surprised it does not have a blue ribbon. A really marvelous shot, well composed, and other elements (diagonal lines) that reall add to the drama. I love the colors, too. Super work!</td>', 'I''m glad this placed well, but surprised it does not have a blue ribbon. A really marvelous shot, well composed, and other elements (diagonal lines) that reall add to the drama. I love the colors, too. Super work!', '2003-06-30 19:30:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(343101, 25602, 6870, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. This was a fun challenge, with lots of great photos. I''m surprised mine did so well and a bit saddened that so many excellent shots placed so far back. I was just outside a window and could not go in, as then my camera would have to have been detoxed (and ruined). But I asked if he could come to the window closer. I liked the dark look, and liked seeing the eyes as a second surprise.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments. This was a fun challenge, with lots of great photos. I''m surprised mine did so well and a bit saddened that so many excellent shots placed so far back. I was just outside a window and could not go in, as then my camera would have to have been detoxed (and ruined). But I asked if he could come to the window closer. I liked the dark look, and liked seeing the eyes as a second surprise.', '2003-06-30 19:35:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(343228, 25969, 8367, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments and votes. They are appreciated.<br/>Jillz - this is what is called bench work. Actually, it''s not really machinery. Just a pneumatic rivet gun and bucking bar. The piece being worked on is in a vise that is attached to my toolbox. Most of the time the work is done directly on the aircraft.<br/>Also, I did try this in B&amp;W as was suggested and it looked pretty good. Thanks for the suggestion.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-07-01 15:40:41.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments and votes. They are appreciated.Jillz - this is what is called bench work. Actually, it''s not really machinery. Just a pneumatic rivet gun and bucking bar. The piece being worked on is in a vise that is attached to my toolbox. Most of the time the work is done directly on the aircraft.Also, I did try this in B&W as was suggested and it looked pretty good. Thanks for the suggestion.', '2003-06-30 22:22:54.000000', '2003-07-01 16:40:41.000000', 0),
