(343722, 25967, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Very nice image, definately different from many of the entries.  The overall composition is very good as is the focus.  This definately meets the challenge and very well portrays someone working.  <br/> <br/>There really isn''t a lot you could do differently other than maybe bring her out of the shadows some it gets to dark to the left side and her shoulder blends in with the background cause of it.<br/> <br/>In all it nicely done and very appealling.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', '*Critique Club* Very nice image, definately different from many of the entries.  The overall composition is very good as is the focus.  This definately meets the challenge and very well portrays someone working.   There really isn''t a lot you could do differently other than maybe bring her out of the shadows some it gets to dark to the left side and her shoulder blends in with the background cause of it. In all it nicely done and very appealling. Anna', '2003-07-01 15:22:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(344023, 25976, 5940, '<td valign="top">I really like the black and white with the subject. It helps to create a very real feeling. If you have any pointers that you can give me on black and white photography I would greatly appreciate it.</td>', 'I really like the black and white with the subject. It helps to create a very real feeling. If you have any pointers that you can give me on black and white photography I would greatly appreciate it.', '2003-07-02 00:00:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(344051, 25929, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>(I am beginning to feel like your  personal critiquer!! :-P)<br/> <br/>I think this shot does an excellent job of showing "at work" in a creative and technically adept way.  The composition works well because the arms lead into the shot to the sander/stripper, and the cord of the stripper presents a nice contrasting angle to it.  The focus looks good as the details are visible, and nothing seems extremely blown out.  The black and white works well, perhaps because it makes the picture simpler.  In color, it could seem distracting, or even "clash" with the different colors present.<br/> <br/>It is a well executed picture, and a good subject, but after looking at it for a while and studying it, I think I finally figured out what kept it from really standing out for me.  It wasn''t noticeable at first, and as I said, I had to study a while to figure it out, but the shadows around the arms bother me.  Overall, the lighting is good, but if you could have shot it without having those shadows, I think it would have made this picture even better. <br/> <br/>Best to you in future challenges!<br/> <br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat (I am beginning to feel like your  personal critiquer!! :-P) I think this shot does an excellent job of showing "at work" in a creative and technically adept way.  The composition works well because the arms lead into the shot to the sander/stripper, and the cord of the stripper presents a nice contrasting angle to it.  The focus looks good as the details are visible, and nothing seems extremely blown out.  The black and white works well, perhaps because it makes the picture simpler.  In color, it could seem distracting, or even "clash" with the different colors present. It is a well executed picture, and a good subject, but after looking at it for a while and studying it, I think I finally figured out what kept it from really standing out for me.  It wasn''t noticeable at first, and as I said, I had to study a while to figure it out, but the shadows around the arms bother me.  Overall, the lighting is good, but if you could have shot it without having those shadows, I think it would have made this picture even better.  Best to you in future challenges! karmat', '2003-07-02 00:28:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(344067, 25881, 1880, '<td valign="top">Ben,<br/> <br/>The more I look at this image the more I appreciate it. You did a good job of saving the details of a  photograph with narrow contrasts. Congratulations on the ribbon and a congrats on a great photograph.  Keep up the good work. - I gave you a 9, this was one of my favorites for the week -  ( PS - I remember the outstanding job you did on the castle photograph that won the blue ribbon. ) <br/> <br/>Bob</td>', 'Ben, The more I look at this image the more I appreciate it. You did a good job of saving the details of a  photograph with narrow contrasts. Congratulations on the ribbon and a congrats on a great photograph.  Keep up the good work. - I gave you a 9, this was one of my favorites for the week -  ( PS - I remember the outstanding job you did on the castle photograph that won the blue ribbon. )  Bob', '2003-07-02 00:36:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(344818, 25827, 7537, '<td valign="top">Sorry about inflicting this image on everyone..... was a bit of a last minute effort, i just found it funny because it was actually a dentists teeth, all be it just after bithday cake!!<br/> <br/>Every comment about how much they would hate it if this was a real dentist made me laugh even more!!!!<br/> <br/>anyway.... sorry again.... but i guess no one will read this anyway...<br/> <br/>Tim</td>', 'Sorry about inflicting this image on everyone..... was a bit of a last minute effort, i just found it funny because it was actually a dentists teeth, all be it just after bithday cake!! Every comment about how much they would hate it if this was a real dentist made me laugh even more!!!! anyway.... sorry again.... but i guess no one will read this anyway... Tim', '2003-07-02 09:08:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(346953, 25953, 4482, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC!<br/> <br/>LIGHTING AND COLOR: I dont see under- or over-ex areas in the photo which makes it appealing to the eye. Nothing to say about the color either, it look fine by me.<br/> <br/>FOCUS: Everthing is in focus.<br/> <br/>COMPOSITION: 1st off I would''ve loved to see him "work" instead of just standing there "not working". He looks more like a spectator. For this reason I don''t think it quite meets the challenge. I also a gree with what Mavrik says... my eye 1st focuses on the man them it searches where to go.... maybe having him closer to the fence and catle would solve this problem.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>Yanik</td>', 'Greetings from the CC! LIGHTING AND COLOR: I dont see under- or over-ex areas in the photo which makes it appealing to the eye. Nothing to say about the color either, it look fine by me. FOCUS: Everthing is in focus. COMPOSITION: 1st off I would''ve loved to see him "work" instead of just standing there "not working". He looks more like a spectator. For this reason I don''t think it quite meets the challenge. I also a gree with what Mavrik says... my eye 1st focuses on the man them it searches where to go.... maybe having him closer to the fence and catle would solve this problem. Keep up the good work! Yanik', '2003-07-04 12:26:32.000000', NULL, 0),
